  "notes": "{立|た}ち{上|あ}がる is a compound verb meaning to stand up or to rise (take action).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}).\n\nCOMPONENTS:\n- {立|た}つ: to stand\n- {上|あ}がる: to go up\n\nTWO MEANINGS:\n1. Physical: to stand up from sitting/lying\n2. Figurative: to rise up, take action, resist\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {椅子|いす}から{立|た}ち{上|あ}がる: to stand up from a chair\n- {困難|こんなん}に{立|た}ち{上|あ}がる: to rise against difficulties\n- {再|ふたた}び{立|た}ち{上|あ}がる: to rise again\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {立|た}ち{上|あ}がる: to stand up (intransitive)\n- {立|た}ち{上|あ}げる: to start up, launch (transitive, e.g., a business)",
